course: dictionary
lesson: 13564
title: Vocabulary in context: inadequate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inadequate means not enough, or not good enough for what is needed. You can see the idea of enough inside the word: adequate means enough, and in- often means not. «The tent was inadequate for the storm, so the campers got soaking wet.» The tent was not good enough for the storm, and the clue soaking wet shows that it failed to keep them dry.
explain: Read the words around the new word and test your meaning. Swap in «not good enough» for inadequate: «The tent was not good enough for the storm» still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: The word can also describe feelings. «Mia said she felt inadequate next to her fast, clever friends.» Here inadequate does not mean the amount of something. It means Mia felt she was not able enough, and that is a sad feeling about yourself.
fact: Inadequate means not enough, or not good enough for what is needed.
fact: «Inadequate food» in a famine means there is not enough food to keep people healthy.
fact: «Feel inadequate» means you feel you are not able or good enough.
fact: You will often see inadequate with the word for, as in «inadequate for the task».
fact: Adequate is the opposite of inadequate: it means enough, or good enough.
exercise: «The data was inadequate, so the scientists could not be sure of their answer.» What does inadequate mean here? | Sent by email | *Not enough for what was needed | Hard to read because of the font | Very big and very colourful
exercise: In a famine, people often had inadequate food. What does this mean? | Food brought from another country | *Not enough food to keep people healthy | Plenty of food for a big feast | Food that tastes very sweet
exercise: Ella says, «I feel inadequate when I do not finish my work.» What feeling is she describing? | Cold and wet | *Not able or good enough about herself | Very happy and proud | Bored, because the work is too easy
test: «The map was inadequate for the long hike, so we got lost.» Which words mean the same as inadequate here? | *Not good enough | Very colourful | Free to use | Brand new
test: Which word is the opposite of inadequate? | *Enough | Late | Rude | Tired
exam: «I feel inadequate because I cannot keep up in the race.» What kind of feeling is this? | Hunger before dinner | Joy at a party | Excitement for the holidays | *Feeling not able enough about yourself
